Fillets: a rounding whose ball rolls on a plane and on a straight edge
parallel to it is the exact cylinder.

A rounding wider than the face beside its edge (a block's top edge rounded
with 5, the block's side 3 high on a plate) rolls on that face's far edge
(0170's rolling ball, BRepBlend_SurfRstConstRad): its ball touches the top
and the side's edge with the plate. Along a straight guide, with the top a
plane and the edge a line parallel to it, the ball's centres lie on a line
and the blend is a cylinder of the radius about it. OCCT walked it and
stored the approximation (a B-spline surface and curves, within the
approximation's tolerance); a later rounding of edges of the result (the
block's front edges, the top's and the arc's) failed on the approximation,
and the stored designs these come from have the cylinder.

ChFi3d_ExactRollOnLine, after CompleteData in the two
ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformSurf of a constant blend rolling on a
restriction: where the rolled-on surface is a plane, the restriction's edge
a line parallel to it and the guide straight and parametrized by its
length, and the walked contacts lie on the exact ones within 1e-3, the
SurfData's surface is replaced by the cylinder (its V the guide's
parameter, its normal on the walked surface's side, trimmed in U to the
section as the walked surface is: code that takes the section from the
surface's bounds, as the ball's centre at an end for 0390, finds it) and its interferences'
curves by the contacts' lines, with exact p-curves on the plane and on a
planar restriction face (else the walked one), on the same parameters;
anything else is left as walked. (The edge on the rolled edge, where the
rounding meets the face beyond at an angle, gets no regularity with 0350.)
